      "textEn": "Until a man is trained and his wife is not his follower. A husband should receive this education at the very beginning of life. Kaumaara Acharetīḥ pāraṁdhāmaṁ dharmāṁ bhagavatāṁ hi (Bhagavata 7.6.1). During Brahmacharya, a bachelor (student) is expected to acquire mastery over bhagvat-dharma (devotion). Therefore, when he marries, and if his wife is devoted to her husband, and she also follows devotion,\nthen the relationship between husband and wife remains very suitable. Without spiritual consciousness,\nthe relationship between husband and wife is not good for mere sensual gratification. Srimad Bhagavatam (12.2.3)\nIt is said that in this Kali Yuga—Dampatyebhiruchirutah—the relationship between husband and wife will be based on sensual desire. Therefore, when both husband and wife are not devoted to Krishna, for them, household life\nis extremely harmful. The autumn lotus-like face, the words are the nectar of hearing.\nThe heart is like a razor, what is the use of the women's? 41. Meaning of the word\n\nSharat—in the autumn season; Padma—lotus-flower; Utsavam—blooming; Vaktram—face; Vachah—word; Cha—also; Shravan—hearing; Kan—ear;\nFor; Amrutam—giving happiness; Hridayam—heart; Kshuradhara—the edge of a sword; Aabham—similar; Striinam—of women;\nKah—who; Veda—knows; Chesthitam—to the character. A woman's face is as attractive and beautiful as a blooming lotus flower in autumn. His words are extremely sweet and pleasing to the ears, but if his heart\nis studied, it will be found that he is as sharp as the edge of a dagger. Who is it, who can know the activities of a woman? Meaning: Kashyap Muni has drawn a very beautiful picture of a woman from a materialistic perspective. Women are famous for their\nbeauty, and in their youth, especially at the age of sixteen or seventeen,\nthey are extremely attractive to men. Therefore, the face of a woman is compared to a winter lotus flower.\nJust as the lotus flower looks extremely beautiful in autumn, in the same way"
