      "textEn": "A woman who has attained puberty is also very attractive. In Sanskrit language, the voice of a woman is\ncalled a female voice because generally she sings and her singing is attractive. Today,\ntomorrow, only the film stars are welcomed. Some of them earn a lot of money just by singing. Therefore, as Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu's teaching is, a woman's music is fatal.\nBecause a sanyasi (ascetic) can become its victim. Renunciation means abandoning the company of women,\nBut if a renunciant listens to the words of a woman and sees her beautiful face, then he\nCertainly becomes attracted to her and falls. Many such examples\nare found. Up to this point, even sage Vishwamitra became a victim of Menaka's charm. Therefore, one who wants to advance spiritually\nshould especially be careful that he does not see the face of a woman and does not\nlisten to her voice.\nTo look at a woman's face and praise her beauty, or to listen to her voice,\nto praise her singing is the certain downfall of a celibate or a renunciant. Therefore, by Kashyap Muni,\nthe description of the parts of a woman is extremely instructive. If a woman's body parts are beautiful, her face is attractive, and her speech is sweet, then she is like a trap for men. The scriptures preach that if such a man comes to serve a woman,\nthen he should be considered a blind well covered with grass. In the fields, there are many such wells, and\nbecause humans are not familiar with them, they fall into them. There are many such instructions. Because\nall the attractions of the world are based on the attraction of women, therefore Kashyap Muni thought that in such a\nsituation, who can know the heart of a woman? Chanakya also advises—\nNever trust a woman or a royal family—“Never trust two types of people—\na politician and a woman.\n” These are the official teachings of the scriptures, therefore, special caution should be exercised in sitting and standing with women. Sometimes our Krishna consciousness