      "textEn": "Males stay together. But devotion to Krishna is for everyone, whether they are men or\nwomen. Shri Krishna himself has said—Whether a woman is a prostitute or a Shudra, she attains the supreme destination—Whether she is a woman, a Shudra,\nor a Vaishya, (let them be Brahmins and Kshatriyas), every being is suitable to return to the abode of God\nif he strictly follows the teachings of his guru and scriptures. Therefore,\nWe would like to request all the members of the Krishna consciousness movement, whether they are women or men, that\nthey should not be attracted to the physical body, but only be attracted to Shri Krishna. Only then will everything be alright.\nOtherwise, fear will remain. Not dear to any woman, with self-control.\nHusbands kill their sons and brothers for the sake of killing them. 42. Meaning of the word\n\nN—No; H—Certainly; Kashchit—Anyone; Priyah—Dear; Striinam—Of women; Anjasa—In reality; Swa-Ashisha—For one's own selfishness; Atmanam—Most dear; Patim—To husband; Putram—To son; Bhrataram—To brother; Va—Or else;\nGhnanti—They kill; Arthae—For one's own selfishness; Ghatayanti—They instigate to kill; Cha—Also. For the fulfillment of their own interests, women treat men as if they\nare their most beloved, but in reality, they have no one dear. Women are considered to be of a very\nsaintly nature, but for their own selfishness, they can even murder their husbands, sons, or brothers,\nor have others do it for them. Meaning: Kashyapa Muni has done a good study of the nature of women. By nature,\nwomen are selfish, therefore they should be protected in every way so that their selfish\nnature does not become apparent.\nWomen need protection by humans. In childhood, a woman's protection should be by her father; in youth, by her husband; and in old age, by her son.\nIt should be by them. This is Manu's order. Their statement is that a woman should not be given freedom in any situation. Women should be protected because of their selfishness"
