      "textEn": "Cannot be revealed. Even in this era, such incidents have occurred in which women have murdered their husbands to avail the benefits of life insurance. This is not criticism of women, but rather a practical study of their\nnature. It is through the body-consciousness that criticism of a woman or a man\nsuch natural tendencies manifest. When a woman or a man's spiritual consciousness increases,\nthen their bodily intellect keeps fading away. We should see all women as spiritual units (I am Brahman) whose only religion is to please Shri Krishna. Then we will not be affected by the qualities of nature arising from holding this body. The Krishna consciousness movement is so beneficial that it can remove the impurities of material nature, which arise from embodiment. Therefore, from the beginning, this is the teaching of the Bhagavad Gita:\nWhether it is a woman or a man, the soul should understand that it is not the body but\nthe soul.\nEvery human being should be interested in the activities of the soul, not the body. Whether\nwoman or man, as long as someone remains inspired by the body-consciousness, there is always a possibility of being misguided.\nThe possibility remains. The soul is sometimes called a man because whether in a woman's attire\nor in a man's attire, he wants to enjoy the pleasures of this material world, and in which there is a tendency to enjoy pleasure,\nthat is called a man. Whether male or female, he is not interested in serving others.\nEvery creature is interested in satisfying its own senses. But Krishna Bhava Namrata\nor Krishna Bhakti provides excellent training to every man or woman. A man\nshould receive training to become a Krishna devotee of the highest order, and a woman\nshould receive training to become a devoted follower of her husband. This will make both of their lives better. I will give it to you as promised, but it will be false there. Even the gods are unable to understand this. 43."
