      "textEn": "Meaning of the word\n\nReported—given word; Dadami—will give; Iti—in this way; Vachah—statement; Tat—that; Na—not; Mrisha—false;\nBhavet—can be; Vadham—murder; Na—not; Arhati—is suitable; Cha—and; Indrah—Indra; Api—also; Tatra—in that context; Idam—this; Upakalpate—is suitable. I have promised him a boon that cannot be violated,\nBut Indra is not worthy of being killed. The solution I have thought of in this situation is\nsuitable. Meaning: Kashyap Muni concluded, \"Diti desires a son who can kill Indra. After all, she is a woman, therefore she is not very clever. I will give him such an education that he, abandoning the idea of killing Indra, himself becomes a Vaishnava, that is, a devotee of Krishna. If she agrees to accept the Vaishnava rules,\nthen her impure heart will surely be purified—Chetodarpanaamarjanam. This is the method of devotion.\nIn Krishna Bhava Namrata, by following the rules of devotion, any person can be made pure because Krishna Bhava Namrata is so powerful\nthat even a person of the most impure class becomes pure and becomes the best Vaishnava. This is the main objective of the movement of Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu. Narottamdas Thakur says—\nBrajendranandan is here, Shachi-Sut is here,\n\nBalram is here at night\n\nThe poor are saved by the name of Hari,\n\nThen the witness awakens-madhai\n\nIn this Kali Yuga, the manifestation of Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu is for the salvation of those fallen souls who\nAlways keep organizing something or the other for material happiness. He has provided this era's humans\nwith an unprecedented opportunity to chant the Hare Krishna Mahamantra, so that they can become completely pure by being freed from all material impurities. Once one becomes a pure Vaishnava, any human being transcends the intellect of the body.\nOne goes beyond that. In this way, Kashyap Muni tried to make his wife a Vaishnavi"
