      "textEn": "Mother's own - of one's mother's sister (aunt); meaning - to be considered; Indra - Indra; Agnya - understanding; Mana-da -\nOne who respects all, O King Parikshit; Shushrushanen - by service; Ashram-stham - residing in the ashram; Ditim - Diti;\nParyacharat - served; Kavih - seeing one's own interest. Oh, King, one who honors all! Indra understood Diti's intention, therefore he\nbegan to think of a way to serve his own interests. Following this argument that self-defense\nis the first law of nature, he wanted to break Diti's vow. Therefore, he\nThe ashram dweller started serving his aunt Diti. Nityam vanaatsu manasah phalamulaasamitkushan. Patrakurmamrudoapcha kale kaal upahart. 57. Meaning of the word\n\nNityam—daily; Vanaat—from the forest; Sumanasah—flowers; Phala—fruits; Moola—roots; Samit—for the Yagya (sacrificial fire);\nKusha—and Kusha grass; Patra—leaves; Angura— buds; Mridah—and soil; Apah—water; Cha—also; Kale Kale—at the right time;\nAt the appropriate time; Upaharta—began to bring;\n.\n\nIndra, every day, brought flowers, fruits, tubers, and offerings for the Yagya from the forest and started serving his aunt. He used to bring Kush, leaves, buds, soil, and water at the right time.\nHe used to bring them. It was coming. And for her, the aperture of the vow, Hari, the king. Prepsu: Pariarchajjimo mrighev mrigakritih. 58. Meaning of the word\n\nEvam—in this way; Tasyah—of that (Diti); Vrat-sthayih—one who observes their vow faithfully; Vrat-\nChidram—a mistake (defect) in observing the vow; Harih—Indra; Nrip—O King; Prepsuha—with the desire to search; Paryacharat—in service;\nGayi—went; Jihmah—deceitful; Mrig-haha—like a deer; Iva—like; Mrig-akritih—like a deer. Oh, King Parikshit! Just as a hunter wears the skin of a deer to kill a deer,\nSimilarly, Indra, from the heart, is the enemy of the sons of Diti, but from the outside,\nHe became a friend and began to serve Diti with great devotion.\nIndra's intention was to deceive Diti by pointing out the error in her vow's\nobservance, but at the same time, he did not want anyone"
